  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: 'Aynuna SAU</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "In modern Saudi Arabia, about 3km inland from the modern fishing port of al\u2011Khuraybah on the Gulf of Aqaba, a pair of ancient Nabatean sites occupy high ground to the northwest of the Wadi Aynuna. Settled since at least the Hellenistic period, Aynuna probably served as a Red Sea port for Petra. Most scholars agree that these sites are to be identified collectively with Leuke Kome, mentioned in Strabo and the Periplus of the Erythraean Sea; however, some other locations have been posited (see Gawlikowski 2022, note 5).",
